<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lutheranism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lutheran</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lutheranism is the branch of Protestant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> based on the teachings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a>, who launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in 1517. Its spread divided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> along religious lines and led to wars ended by settlements such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-augsburg">Peace of Augsburg</a>. Lutheranism became the state religion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> and gained followers in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>.</p></div>
